From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: cam: cpas: skip camnoc fill-level monitor reads on Titan 170 v1xx

Root cause of the SoC-wide NoC wedge at IFE bring-up on sdm845:
cam_cpas_update_monitor_array() unconditionally reads three "camnoc
fill level" debug registers at CAMNOC offsets 0xA20/0x1420/0x1A20.
Those offsets belong to the newer CAMNOC layouts this camera_kt tree
targets (e.g. qcm6490 / Titan 170 V200); on sdm845's Titan 170 V110
CAMNOC they hit a non-responding region, the AXI read never completes,
and the whole NoC (and every CPU behind it) hangs -- zero dmesg, RCU
stalls, NMI-dead cores.

The monitor is only invoked from cam_cpas_hw_update_axi_vote (and
vote_level paths), never from cpas_start, which is why sensor probing
and full SpectraMaster init always survived and the first BW-config
blob of an IFE start (the first hw_update_axi_vote ever) always died.
Instrumented run evidence: every layer of the bw chain down through
icc_set_bw completes (rc=0), then the trail ends exactly between
apply_client_axi_vote returning and hw_update_axi_vote's monitor call.

Gate the three reads off for Titan 170 V100/V110/V120, mirroring the
existing V580-only guard for fill levels 3 and 4. The fields stay zero
in the monitor dump on these parts.
---

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_cpas/cam_cpas_hw.c b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_cpas/cam_cpas_hw.c
index 08b70d9..ab43e53 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_cpas/cam_cpas_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_cpas/cam_cpas_hw.c
@@ -2062,12 +2062,16 @@ static void cam_cpas_update_monitor_array(struct cam_hw_info *cpas_hw,
 		entry->be_mnoc = cam_io_r_mb(rpmh_base + be_mnoc_offset);
 	}
 
-	entry->camnoc_fill_level[0] = cam_io_r_mb(
-		soc_info->reg_map[reg_camnoc].mem_base + 0xA20);
-	entry->camnoc_fill_level[1] = cam_io_r_mb(
-		soc_info->reg_map[reg_camnoc].mem_base + 0x1420);
-	entry->camnoc_fill_level[2] = cam_io_r_mb(
-		soc_info->reg_map[reg_camnoc].mem_base + 0x1A20);
+	if ((cpas_hw->soc_info.hw_version != CAM_CPAS_TITAN_170_V100) &&
+		(cpas_hw->soc_info.hw_version != CAM_CPAS_TITAN_170_V110) &&
+		(cpas_hw->soc_info.hw_version != CAM_CPAS_TITAN_170_V120)) {
+		entry->camnoc_fill_level[0] = cam_io_r_mb(
+			soc_info->reg_map[reg_camnoc].mem_base + 0xA20);
+		entry->camnoc_fill_level[1] = cam_io_r_mb(
+			soc_info->reg_map[reg_camnoc].mem_base + 0x1420);
+		entry->camnoc_fill_level[2] = cam_io_r_mb(
+			soc_info->reg_map[reg_camnoc].mem_base + 0x1A20);
+	}
 
 	if (cpas_hw->soc_info.hw_version == CAM_CPAS_TITAN_580_V100) {
 		entry->camnoc_fill_level[3] = cam_io_r_mb(
